# Events on the climb between the Tsolenka Pass and the Amber Temple (data/random_encounters/amber_temple_road.json).
# Each plays on the road map amber_temple_road; when it ends without a fight, the journey goes on.

~ whiteout
Narrator: The wind turns, and the mountain disappears. Snow comes sideways, thick as wool, and the person in front of you becomes a grey shape, then a voice, then nothing.
* [Survival DC 15] Rope together and find the cairns. -> whiteout_ok | whiteout_lost
* Dig in behind a boulder and wait it out. -> whiteout_wait

~ whiteout_ok
Narrator: Cairn to cairn, roped hand to hand, you find the path. When the snow lifts, you are further on than you'd have dared to hope.
-> END

~ whiteout_lost
time +120
Narrator: You walk for an hour and come back to your own footprints. By the time the snow lifts, the light has moved a long way across the sky.
interject name:godrick_pendlebrook: Everybody here? Shout if you're not. ...Right. Nobody's shouted. Good.
-> END

~ whiteout_wait
time +180
Narrator: You huddle in the lee of a boulder while the mountain screams over your heads. It passes, eventually. Everything up here passes, except the cold.
-> END

~ expedition
if flag.amber_road_expedition_found
-> END
endif
set amber_road_expedition_found
Narrator: Off the path, half buried, a ring of tents has been crushed flat by old snow. Inside, a party of climbers sits where the cold found them, still holding their cups.
Narrator: One has a journal open on his knee. The last page reads: "Tomorrow the temple. Petra says she can hear it already. She says it knows our names."
* Take what they won't need. -> expedition_take
* [Religion DC 12] Say the words for the dead over them. -> expedition_rites | expedition_rites_plain
* Leave them in peace. -> END

~ expedition_take
give potion_of_healing 2
give climbers_kit
gold +30
Narrator: You take their potions, their purse and their ropes, and you tell them, out loud, that you'll put it all to good use. It seems only polite.
approve kip_smudgewick -1 liriel_dawnsong -1: You went through a frozen expedition's packs
-> END

~ expedition_rites
Narrator: You say the words. When you look back from the next bend, the snow has covered them over gently, like a sheet drawn up by someone who loved them.
interject name:liriel_dawnsong: Be at peace. Nobody should have to wait so long to be told they may stop.
approve liriel_dawnsong +2 godrick_pendlebrook +1: You said the words over a frozen expedition
-> END

~ expedition_rites_plain
Narrator: You stumble over the old words, but you say them. The wind takes them. Perhaps it carries them where they need to go.
-> END
